        <article class="lesson-article">
            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 6</span><h1>Cancellation Tokens</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>30 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Cooperative Cancellation</h2>
                    <p>CancellationToken enables cooperative cancellation—operations must check for cancellation and stop gracefully.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Create a cancellation token source
using var cts = new CancellationTokenSource();

// Cancel after 5 seconds
cts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

// Or cancel manually
cts.Cancel();

// Pass token to async methods
await DoWorkAsync(cts.Token);</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Responding to Cancellation</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public async Task ProcessAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    foreach (var item in items)
    {
        // Check for cancellation
        cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
        
        // Or check without throwing
        if (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Cleanup and exit gracefully
            break;
        }
        
        // Pass token to nested operations
        await ProcessItemAsync(item, cancellationToken);
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Timeout Pattern</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public async Task&lt;Data&gt; GetWithTimeoutAsync(TimeSpan timeout)
{
    using var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(timeout);
    
    try
    {
        return await GetDataAsync(cts.Token);
    }
    catch (OperationCanceledException) when (cts.IsCancellationRequested)
    {
        throw new TimeoutException($"Operation timed out after {timeout}");
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Linked Cancellation</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Combine multiple cancellation sources
public async Task ProcessAsync(CancellationToken externalToken)
{
    using var timeoutCts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5));
    
    // Cancel if either external OR timeout occurs
    using var linkedCts = CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource(
        externalToken, 
        timeoutCts.Token);
    
    await DoWorkAsync(linkedCts.Token);
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Cancellation is cooperative—check the token!</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use CancelAfter for timeouts.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Always pass tokens through async call chains.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Link tokens to combine cancellation sources.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
